Not quite.  "Magic cancellation" is the property of some kinds of armor, 
notably cloaks, to deflect certain monster special attacks.  The most 
important is level drain, but paralyis, slime, and disenchanting attacks 
are also affected, among many others.

Your only armor with MC is the apron, which only cancels about 1/3 of 
special attacks.  An apron is very stylish, however if you have poison 
resistance intrinsically it's not that helpful.  In that case you might 
wish for a cloak of displacement (only if you are not intrinsically 
invisible) which cancels about 2/3 of the concerned special attacks, or 
a cloak of protection or elven cloak, which would cancel about 98%.
(In fact, there should be no need to wish for an elven cloak; my 
dungeons are always littered with the things.)

I'd say that magic markers are a better wish.  And an apron is *very* 
stylish.  Just be careful around those vampires.

